"https://milton-keynes.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-08","committee":"Cabinet","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://milton-keynes.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-09","committee":"BMKFA - Executive Committee","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://milton-keynes.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-16","committee":"Standing Advisory Council on Religious Education","time":"4.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://milton-keynes.moderngov.co.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Internal audit resource constraints escalated in September have been addressed by filling three vacancies","lead":"Internal audit capacity is essential to detect control breakdowns and financial irregularities early \u2014 resource gaps create audit blind spots that increase financial and operational risk","iso":"2026-09-23","paper_title":"Audit Committee Annual Report 2025-26","paper_url":"https://milton-keynes.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s30674/30674.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Two internal audits issued limited assurance opinions, indicating significant control issues","lead":"Control weaknesses affect the reliability of financial reporting and the council's ability to safeguard assets \u2014 a lender needs to know whether these issues affect financial controls, expenditure, or income","iso":"2026-09-23","paper_title":"Audit Committee Annual Report 2025-26","paper_url":"https://milton-keynes.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s30674/30674.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Landlord Incentive Scheme: deposit recovery process in progress via new bond scheme; rent guarantee payment recovery unresolved with no income recovery officers assigned","lead":"Both create direct financial risk to the council. Deposits and guarantees represent cash exposures; lack of recovery process means losses are deferred or unrecorded. The move to a bond scheme acknowledges prior losses.","iso":"2026-09-22","paper_title":"22 Sept 26 AC - IA Progress Update Annex C - Actions Tracker","paper_url":"https://milton-keynes.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s30719/30719.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-23","committee":"Council","paper_title":"Audit Committee Annual Report 2025-26","paper_url":"https://milton-keynes.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s30674/30674.pdf","headline":"Internal audit resource constraints escalated in September have been addressed by filling three vacancies","detail":"The committee discussed in September that internal audit could not fully deliver its plan due to stretched resources. By February 2026, three positions had been filled and a framework for specialist audits put in place. The committee had sought assurance that resource levels would improve in the near term, which appears to have been achieved.","category":"governance","matters":"Internal audit capacity is essential to detect control breakdowns and financial irregularities early \u2014 resource gaps create audit blind spots that increase financial and operational risk","figures":"three positions had been filled","quote":"At the September meeting, the challenges to delivery of the Audit Plan due to stretched resources was discussed with Committee seeking assurance that levels of resource available will be improved in the very near future. At the February 2026 meeting it was noted that three positions had been filled, and a framework arrangement put in place for delivery of specialist Internal audits.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-23","committee":"Council","paper_title":"Audit Committee Annual Report 2025-26","paper_url":"https://milton-keynes.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s30674/30674.pdf","headline":"Two internal audits issued limited assurance opinions, indicating significant control issues","detail":"During 2025-26, internal audit issued two reports with limited assurance opinions. The committee defines limited assurance as meaning auditors identified significant control issues presenting high risk to the control environment, or the control environment had not operated as intended. Full reports were circulated to committee members but this summary does not specify which areas were affected.","category":"audit","matters":"Control weaknesses affect the reliability of financial reporting and the council's ability to safeguard assets \u2014 a lender needs to know whether these issues affect financial controls, expenditure, or income","figures":"Two limited assurance audit opinion reports","quote":"Two limited assurance opinion reports were issued during the year and circulated to Committee members.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-22","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"22 Sept 26 AC - IA Progress Update Annex C - Actions Tracker","paper_url":"https://milton-keynes.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s30719/30719.pdf","headline":"Landlord Incentive Scheme: deposit recovery process in progress via new bond scheme; rent guarantee payment recovery unresolved with no income recovery officers assigned","detail":"Two financial recovery gaps in the Landlord Incentive Scheme. Deposits: A new Deposit Bond Scheme is being drawn to replace direct cash deposits held by the council to 'greatly reduce MKCC losses', suggesting prior losses from the cash deposit approach. Rent guarantees: No process exists to recover rent guarantee payments made on behalf of tenants who default. The council lacks dedicated income recovery officers in the service; as of July 2026, discussion is ongoing about whether recovery should transfer to the council's debt recovery team.","category":"income","matters":"Both create direct financial risk to the council. Deposits and guarantees represent cash exposures; lack of recovery process means losses are deferred or unrecorded. The move to a bond scheme acknowledges prior losses.","figures":"Deposit Bond Scheme being drawn to replace cash deposits. Rent guarantee recovery: no income recovery officers assigned. Due date 30/09/27.","quote":"A new Deposit Bond Scheme is currently being drawn to replace the current cash deposits that are paid, and this should ensure that MKCC losses are greatly reduced.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-22","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"22 Sept 26 AC - IA Progress Update Annex C - Actions Tracker","paper_url":"https://milton-keynes.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s30719/30719.pdf","headline":"Structures inspection compliance improvements in progress since October 2024; original target now 18 months overdue","detail":"A significant audit finding on delays in structures inspection completion and approval remains in progress with an original target of 31 October 2024 revised to 12 December 2025, and still not closed as of July 2026. Successive updates through 2025\u201326 report incremental improvements in compliance rates and process adjustments (e.g. extending planning/inspection cycle from 30 days to 2 months from February 2026), indicating the council is still working to implement resolution.","category":"governance","matters":"Inspection compliance directly affects asset safety and risk management. Sustained delays in achieving basic compliance, with multiple missed targets and continued remediation, suggest resource constraints or process challenges that have persisted for over 18 months.","figures":"Original target 31/10/24. Revised to 12/12/25. Still in progress July 2026. Planning/inspection cycle extended 30 days to 2 months February 2026.","quote":"The monitoring that has occurred since the last update has shown that the 30 day target for inspectors to plan & inspect has proved to be too inflexible and a 2 month planning and inspection target will be introduced from February 2026","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-22","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"22 Sept 26 AC - IA Progress Update Annex C - Actions Tracker","paper_url":"https://milton-keynes.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s30719/30719.pdf","headline":"Education, Health and Care Plans not issued within statutory 20-week timescale; backlog project extended from January to October 2026 now dependent on agency support","detail":"The council is not meeting the statutory 20-week timescale for issuing EHCPs. A backlog clearance project originally targeted for 30 January 2026 has been extended to 31 October 2026. As of July 2026, Educational Psychologists' assessment work is completed on time, but plan-writing is the bottleneck. Agency workers were approved to start 10 August 2026 to write plans, with progress review at end October.","category":"demand","matters":"Failure to meet statutory timescales in SEND support creates legal and reputational risk for the council and indicates demand-capacity mismatch. Extended backlog management requiring agency spend demonstrates sustained pressure on permanent resources.","figures":"Original backlog target 30/01/26. Revised to 31/10/26. Agency workers approved start date 10/08/26. Review end October 2026.","quote":"The writing of the plans is the part of the assessement process we now need to address. A plan is being progressed to utilise agency workers to write the plans to clear the final backlog.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-08"},"name":"Milton Keynes UA","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-21","since_iso":"2026-08-22","distress":false,"headline":"Waste Recovery Plant contractor support \u00a3700k annually expires October 2026 during transition to new commercial contract.","lead":"Contract transitions for critical infrastructure carry implementation risk, particularly for a facility with recent catastrophic failures. A lender would want assurance that the new commercial model reduces rather than increases the council's financial\u2026","also":["30 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Audit Committee on 2026-09-22","n_findings":31,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Strategic Risk Register - Annex B -Strategic Risk Register","top_paper_url":"https://milton-keynes.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s30568/30568.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":142,"news_drafts_total":3}}